\p{So}

##{I = \int_{C_1} + \int_{C_2} + \int_{C_3},}

\p{with #{\int_{C_1} = O\big( \frac{e^{xu_1}}{x} \big)} and #{\int_{C_3} = O\big( \frac{e^{xu_2}}{x} \big)} by Laplace. Is #{\int_{C_2}} small? Take #{C_1} and #{C_3} to #{\infty} and join them up with an infinitely short #{C_2}, which will contribute nothing.}
